{title: Jesus Saves (We Have Heard the Joyful Sound)}
{artist: Priscilla J. Owens / William J. Kirkpatrick}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Upbeat}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Baptist Hymnnal (Nashville, Tennessee: Convention Press, 1975), # 277)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]We have heard the joyful sound:
[G]Jesus saves! Jesus [D7]saves!
[D7]Spread the [G]tidings all around:
[G]Jesus [D7]saves! Jesus [G]saves!
[C]Bear the news to every land,
[G]Climb the mountains, cross the [D]waves;
[D]Onward! [G]’tis our Lord’s com[C]mand;
[G]Jesus [D7]saves! Jesus [G]saves!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Waft it on the rolling tide:
[G]Jesus saves! Jesus [D7]saves!
[D7]Tell to [G]sinners far and wide:
[G]Jesus [D7]saves! Jesus [G]saves!
[C]Sing, you islands of the sea;
[G]Echo back, you ocean [D]caves;
[D]Earth shall [G]keep her jubi[C]lee:
[G]Jesus [D7]saves! Jesus [G]saves!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Sing above the battle strife:
[G]Jesus saves! Jesus [D7]saves!
[D7]By His [G]death and endless life
[G]Jesus [D7]saves! Jesus [G]saves!
[C]Shout it brightly through the gloom,
[G]When the heart for mercy [D]craves;
[D]Sing in [G]triumph o’er the [C]tomb:
[G]Jesus [D7]saves! Jesus [G]saves!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Give the winds a mighty voice:
[G]Jesus saves! Jesus [D7]saves!
[D7]Let the [G]nations now rejoice:
[G]Jesus [D7]saves! Jesus [G]saves!
[C]Shout salvation full and free;
[G]Highest hills and deepest [D]caves;
[D]This our [G]song of victo[C]ry:
[G]Jesus [D7]saves! Jesus [G]saves!
{end_of_verse}
